\v 8 Eytan's¦187689 \add #son¦187688\add* was¦187690 Azaryah¦187690.
\s1 King David's ancestors
\rem /s1 The Family Tree of King David; From Judah's Grandson Hezron to David
\p
\v 9 Hetsron¦187693 had three sons¦187692: Yerahme'el¦187700, Ram¦187703, and¦187704 Keluvay¦187706.\f + \fr 2:9 \ft In the Hebrew, ‘Keluvay’ is called ‘Kalev’ (Caleb) below.\f*
\rem /s2 From Ram Son of Hezron
\p
\v 10 Ram¦187708 was the father¦187709 of Aminadav¦187712, and¦187713 Aminadav¦187713 was the father¦187714 of Nahshon¦187717—a leader¦187718 of¦187718 the¦187719 \add ≈tribe\add* of¦187719 Yehudah¦187720 \add !(Judah¦187720)\add*.
\v 11 Nahshon¦187722 was the father¦187723 of Salma¦187726. Salma¦187727 was the father¦187728 of Boaz¦187731.
\v 12 Boaz¦187733 was the father¦187734 of Oved¦187737. Oved¦187738 was the father¦187739 of Yishay¦187742 \add !(Jesse¦187742)\add*.
\v 13 Yishay¦187744 had his¦187748 son Eliav¦187751 first, Avinadav¦187752 second¦187753, Shimea¦187754 third¦187755.
\v 14 Netanel¦187757 fourth¦187758, Raday¦187759 fifth¦187760,
\v 15 Otsem¦187762 sixth¦187763, then David¦187764 \add ≈last\add*.
\v 16 Their¦187767 sisters¦187767 were¦187769 Tseruyah¦187769 and¦187770 Avigayil¦187770. Tseruyah's¦187772 three¦187778 sons¦187771 were¦187773 Avishay¦187773, Yoav¦187774 \add !(Joab¦187774)\add*, and¦187775 Asahel.
\v 17 Avigayil¦187780 had Amasa¦187784. Amasa's¦187786 father¦187785 was¦187787 Yeter¦187787, a descendant of Yishmael \add !(Ishmael)\add*.
