\p
\v 18 Hetsron's¦187793 \add third\add* son Kalev¦187790 \add !(Caleb¦187790)\add* had sons¦187791 with¦187795 Azuvah¦187797, one of \add &his¦187798\add* wives¦187798. The sons¦187803 were¦187803 Yesher¦187804, Shovav¦187805, and¦187806 Ardon¦187806. (The other wife's name was Yerieot¦187801.)
\v 19 When¦187808 Azuvah¦187809 died¦187808, Kalev¦187813 married Efrat¦187816, and¦187817 they had a son named Hur¦187821.
\v 20 Hur¦187823 was the father¦187824 of Uri¦187827, and¦187828 Uri¦187828 was the father¦187829 of Betsalel¦187832.
\p
\v 21 Later¦187835, when Hetsron¦187837 was¦187848 sixty¦187850 years¦187851 old, he¦187836 \add ≈had sexual intercourse\add* with a daughter¦187840 of¦187840 Makir¦187842 from the¦187843 region of¦187843 Gilead¦187844 and¦187845 married her¦187846. \add @Hetsron's new wife\add* gave¦187852 birth¦187852 to¦187853 \add their son\add* Seguv¦187856.
\v 22 Seguv¦187858 was the father¦187859 of Yair¦187862, and¦187863 \add @Yair\add* controlled twenty-three cities¦187868 in¦187869 the¦187870 Gilead¦187870 region¦187869.
\v 23 \add ≈But¦187872\add* Geshur¦187873 and¦187875 Aram¦187875 captured¦187872 Havot-Ya'ir¦187879 and Kenat¦187883 from¦187880 them¦187880, plus¦187884 \add ≈their surrounding towns\add*—sixty¦187887 towns \add in all,\add* \add ≈populated by\add* descendants¦187892 of¦187892 Makir¦187893 (the¦187894 father¦187894 of¦187894 Gilead¦187896).
\v 24 After¦187898 Hetsron's¦187901 death¦187899 in¦187902 Kalev¦187902-Efratah¦187903, \add *his\add* wife¦187904 Aviyah¦187906 gave¦187907 birth¦187907 to¦187908 his son Ashur¦187911 \add !(Assyria¦187911)\add*, the¦187912 father¦187912 of¦187912 Tekoa¦187913.
\s1 Yerahme'el's descendants
\rem /s1 Descendants of Hezron's Son Jerahmeel; The Descendants of Jerahmeel
\rem /s2 Jerahmeel Son of Hezron
\p
\v 25 Hetsron's¦187920 oldest son was Yerahme'el¦187918 \add and\add* his sons¦187916 were¦187915 Ram¦187923 (the oldest), Bunah¦187924, Oren¦187925, Otsem¦187926, and Ahiyah¦187927.
\v 26 Yerahme'el¦187932 had another¦187931 wife¦187930 named¦187933 Atarah¦187934. She¦187935 was¦187936 the¦187936 mother¦187936 of¦187936 Onam¦187937.
\v 27 The¦187941 sons¦187941 of¦187941 Yerahme'el's¦187945 oldest son, Ram¦187943, were¦187940 Ma'ats¦187946, Yamin¦187947, and¦187948 Eker¦187948.
\v 28 Onam's¦187953 sons¦187951 were¦187950 Shamay¦187954 and¦187955 Yada¦187955, and¦187956 Shamay's¦187957 sons were¦187958 Nadav¦187958 and¦187959 Avishur¦187959.
\p
\v 29 Avishur's¦187963 wife¦187962 was¦187964 Avihayil¦187964, and¦187965 \add ≈their sons were\add* Ahban¦187969 and¦187970 Molid¦187972.
\v 30 Nadav's¦187975 sons were¦187976 Seled¦187976 and¦187977 Apayim¦187977. (Seled¦187979 died¦187978 childless.)
\v 31 Apayim's¦187985 son was¦187986 Yishei¦187986, Yishei's¦187988 son was¦187989 Sheshan¦187989, and¦187990 Sheshan's¦187991 son was¦187992 Ahlay¦187992.
\p
\v 32 The¦187994 sons¦187994 of¦187995 Shamay's¦187997 brother¦187996 Yada¦187995 were¦187998 Yeter¦187998 and¦187999 Yonatan¦187999 \add !(Jonathan¦187999)\add*. (Yeter¦188001 died¦188000 childless.)
\v 33 Yonatan's¦188007 sons were¦188008 Pelet¦188008 and¦188009 Zaza¦188009.
\m Those¦188010 were¦188011 the¦188012 descendants¦188012 of¦188012 Yerahme'el¦188013.
\p
\v 34 Sheshan¦188018 had no sons¦188019, only daughters¦188023. \add *He¦188024\add* had a¦188025 \add male\add* servant¦188025 from¦188026 Mitsrayim¦188026 \add !(Egypt¦188026)\add* whose name¦188027 was¦188028 Yarha¦188028,
\v 35 and¦188030 Sheshan¦188031 gave¦188030 his¦188034 daughter¦188034 to¦188035 \add *him¦188035\add* for¦188037 a¦188037 wife¦188037, and¦188038 \add ≈they had a son\add* Atay¦188042.
\v 36 Atay¦188044 was the father¦188045 of Natan¦188048 \add !(Nathan¦188048)\add*, and¦188049 Natan¦188049 was the father¦188050 of Zavad¦188053.
\v 37 Zavad¦188055 was the father¦188056 of Eflal¦188059, and¦188060 Eflal¦188060 was the father¦188061 of Oved¦188064.
\v 38 Oved¦188066 was the father¦188067 of Yehu¦188070 \add !(Jehu¦188070)\add*, and¦188071 Yehu¦188071 was the father¦188072 of Azaryah¦188075.
\v 39 Azaryah¦188077 was the father¦188078 of Helets¦188081, and¦188082 Helets¦188082 was the father¦188083 of Eleasah¦188086.
\v 40 Eleasah¦188088 was the father¦188089 of Sismay¦188092, and¦188093 Sismay¦188093 was the father¦188094 of Shalum¦188097.
\v 41 Shalum¦188099 was the father¦188100 of Yekamyah¦188103, and¦188104 Yekamyah¦188104 was the father¦188105 of Elishama¦188108.
