\s1 The eastern warriors
\rem /s1 The Tribes East of the Jordan; The Armies of the Eastern Tribes
\p
\v 18 There were 44,760 warriors descended¦189346 from¦189354 \add ≈strong¦189358\add* men¦189359 in the¦189346 tribes of¦189346 Re'uven¦189348 and¦189349 Gad and¦189350 the¦189350 \add eastern\add* half¦189350 of¦189350 the¦189351 tribe¦189351 of¦189351 Menasheh¦189353 \add !(Manasseh¦189353)\add*. They all carried¦189360 \add #shields¦189361\add* and¦189362 \add #swords¦189362\add*, and¦189363 \add #bows¦189364\add* and arrows, and were¦189365 all trained¦189365 to fight¦189375 in battles.
\v 19 They¦189377 went to war¦189378 against the¦189381 Hagrim¦189381, Yetur¦189382, Nafish¦189383, and¦189384 Nodav¦189384,
\v 20 and¦189386 were¦189386 helped¦189386 because¦189393 they¦189395 called¦189395 out¦189395 to God in¦189396 the battle¦189396. \add ≈So¦189397\add* with God answering their prayers¦189397 because¦189399 of their trust¦189401 in¦189402 him¦189402, they \add ≈were able to defeat\add* the Hagrim¦189390 and¦189391 their \add ≈allies\add*.
\v 21 They¦189404 captured¦189404 their¦189405 livestock¦189405, including 50,000 camels¦189406, 250,000 sheep¦189409, and 2,000 donkeys¦189413, as well as 100,000 people¦189415,
\v 22 because¦189420 many¦189423 were¦189426 killed¦189422 \add ≈as a result of God's¦189426 assistance\add*. Then¦189428 they¦189428 lived¦189428 in¦189429 that \add ≈area\add* until¦189430 the¦189432 exile¦189432.
