\v 11 \add ≈So¦196866\add* Gad¦196867 went¦196866 to¦196868 David¦196870 and¦196871 told¦196871 him¦196872, “Yahweh¦196876 says¦196875 that you¦196879 must choose \add one of these punishments\add*:
\v 12 either three¦196883 years¦196884 of famine¦196885, or three¦196888 months¦196889 of being¦196890 overcome by your¦196895 enemies'¦196895 \add ≈armies\add*, or three¦196900 days¦196901 of¦196902 Yahweh's¦196903 ‘sword’ of pestilence¦196904 in the¦196905 country and¦196906 Yahweh's¦196907 messenger¦196906 \add ≈bringing¦196917 destruction¦196908\add* across all¦196909 of¦196911 Yisrael's¦196912 territory¦196911. \add ≈So¦196913 now¦196913, tell me what¦196915 answer I¦196917 should take¦196917\add* back¦196917 to the¦196920 one¦196920 who¦196920 sent¦196920 me¦196920.”
