\v 14 \add ≈So¦196951\add* Yahweh¦196952 \add ≈sent a¦196953 disease¦196953\add* throughout Yisrael¦196954, and¦196955 seventy¦196957 thousand¦196958 Israeli¦196956 men \add ≈died\add*.
\v 15 Then¦196961 God sent¦196961 a messenger¦196964 to¦196966 destroy¦196967 Yerushalem¦196966 \add !(Jerusalem¦196966)\add*, and¦196968 \add ≈while the disease was¦196968 still spreading,\add* Yahweh¦196970 \add ≈looked¦196969 down\add* and¦196971 relented about the¦196974 tragedy, and¦196975 he¦196975 told¦196975 the¦196977 destroying¦196977 messenger, “Enough¦196978! Now \add ≈stop what you're doing\add*.” Now Yahweh's¦196983 messenger \add happened to be\add* standing¦196984 at the¦196987 threshing¦196987 floor¦196987 belonging to Ornan¦196988 the¦196989 Yevusi¦196989.
\p
\v 16 \add As\add* David¦196993 \add ≈looked up¦196992\add*, he¦196997 saw¦196997 Yahweh's¦197001 messenger¦197000 standing¦197002 between¦197003 the¦197004 earth¦197004 and¦197005 the¦197006 heavens¦197006, holding his¦197007 sword¦197007 stretched¦197010 out¦197010 over¦197011 Yerushalem¦197013. Then¦197014 David¦197015 and¦197016 the¦197016 elders¦197016, who were \add all\add* dressed in¦197018 sackcloth¦197018, fell¦197014 \add ≈to their knees and bowed their faces¦197021 to the ground\add*.
\v 17 Then¦197023 David¦197024 \add ≈asked\add* God, “Wasn't it¦197023 me myself who said¦197023 to count¦197031 the people¦197032? It's me who¦197036 \add ≈disobeyed¦197038 and¦197039 clearly did what was wrong\add*, but¦197041 these¦197041 sheep¦197042, what¦197043 have¦197044 they¦197044 done¦197044? Yahweh¦197045 my god, please¦197048 \add ≈direct your¦197049 punishment\add* against me¦197050 and¦197051 \add ≈my¦197052 extended family¦197051\add*, but¦197053 \add ≈don't¦197054 continue this\add* \add ≈deadly disease¦197055\add* on¦197053 your people.”
