\p
\v 18 Then¦197058 Yahweh's¦197059 messenger¦197058 told¦197060 Gad¦197063 to¦197064 tell¦197064 David¦197065 that¦197066 \add *he¦197069\add* should \add ≈build\add* an¦197071 altar¦197071 to¦197072 Yahweh¦197072 at Ornan¦197074 the¦197073 Yevusi's¦197075 threshing¦197073 floor¦197073.
\v 19 \add ≈So¦197077\add* David¦197078 went up \add to that place when he heard\add* \add ≈Gad's¦197081 message¦197079 that¦197082 was delivered\add* in¦197084 Yahweh's¦197085 name¦197084.
\v 20 ⇔\add ≈Meanwhile,\add* Ornan was threshing¦197098 wheat¦197099, and¦197087 \add *he¦197088\add* turned¦197087 and¦197089 saw¦197089 \add &Yahweh's¦197092\add* messenger¦197092, and he and his four¦197093 sons¦197094 who were¦197096 with¦197095 him¦197095 \add quickly\add* hid¦197096 \add ≈behind something\add*.
\v 21 \add ≈When¦197101 David¦197102 arrived¦197101 there,\add* Ornan saw¦197108 \add *him¦197111\add* and¦197112 left¦197112 the¦197115 threshing¦197115 floor¦197115 and \add ≈knelt\add* in front of David¦197117, bowing¦197116 \add &his\add* face¦197118 to¦197119 the¦197119 ground¦197119.
\v 22 Then¦197121 David¦197122 \add ≈asked¦197121\add* Ornan¦197125, “Give¦197126 me¦197128 this place¦197129 with its threshing¦197130 floor¦197130, and I'll¦197131 build¦197131 an¦197134 altar¦197134 to¦197135 Yahweh¦197135 on it. \add ≈Sell it to¦197139 me¦197139\add* at the full¦197137 price¦197136, so¦197140 the¦197141 \add ≈deadly disease¦197141 affecting\add* the¦197143 people¦197143 will be stopped¦197140.”
\p
\v 23 “My¦197154 master¦197154 the¦197155 king¦197155, take¦197150 \add ≈anything you want\add*,” Ornan¦197146 \add ≈replied¦197145\add*. “Listen, I'll¦197159 donate the¦197160 cattle¦197160 for¦197161 the burnt offerings¦197161, and¦197162 the¦197162 threshing sledges¦197162 for¦197163 firewood¦197163, and¦197164 the¦197164 wheat¦197164 for¦197165 the offering¦197165—all \add ≈at no charge\add*.”
