\p
\v 2 Then¦197291 David¦197292 said¦197291 to¦197293 gather¦197293 the¦197296 foreigners who¦197297 \add ≈lived\add* in¦197298 Yisrael¦197299 \add !(Israel¦197299)\add*, and¦197300 he¦197300 assigned¦197300 \add ≈them the job of\add* hewing¦197304 out cut¦197302 stones¦197303 to¦197305 build¦197305 the¦197306 residence for God.
\v 3 \add *He\add* prepared¦197316 a large quantity of iron¦197309 for the¦197313 door¦197313 \add ≈hinges and¦197315 fittings\add*, so¦197318 much brass that it couldn't be¦197320 weighed¦197321,
\v 4 and¦197323 innumerable cedar¦197324 logs that the¦197329 Tsidonim¦197329 \add !(Sidonians¦197329)\add* and¦197330 the¦197330 Tsorim¦197330 \add !(Tyrians¦197330)\add* brought¦197328 in¦197333 for David¦197334.
\v 5 David¦197338 said¦197337, “My¦197340 son¦197340 Shelomoh¦197339 \add !(Solomon¦197339)\add* is¦197341 young¦197341 and¦197342 not capable, and¦197343 the¦197343 house¦197343 to¦197344 be built¦197344 for¦197345 Yahweh¦197345 must be¦197346 \add ≈impressive for¦197349 the sake of his reputation¦197349\add* and¦197350 honour¦197350 everywhere¦197351, \add so\add* I'll¦197354 prepare¦197354 for it¦197356 now.” \add ≈So¦197357\add* David¦197358 did a lot of¦197360 \add ≈preparation¦197357\add* before¦197360 \add ≈he died¦197361\add*.
\rem /s1 David's Charge to Solomon and the Leaders
\p
\v 6 Then¦197363 \add @David¦197363\add* called¦197363 for his¦197365 son¦197365 Shelomoh¦197364, and¦197366 ordered¦197366 him¦197366 to¦197367 build¦197367 a¦197368 residence for¦197369 Yisrael's¦197371 god¦197370 Yahweh¦197369.
\v 7 David¦197375 told¦197374 \add *him¦197376\add*, “My¦197377 son¦197377, I¦197379 wanted to¦197384 build¦197384 a¦197385 temple¦197385 to honour my¦197388 god¦197388 Yahweh¦197387,\x + \xo 22:7-10: \xt 2Sam 7:1-16; 1Ch 17:1-14.\x*
\v 8 \add ≈but¦197390\add* Yahweh¦197394 \add ≈gave me¦197391 this message¦197392\add*, ‘You've¦197398 fought a lot of battles¦197399 and shed a large¦197400 amount of blood, \add so\add* you¦197401 won't¦197402 be the one who'll build¦197404 a¦197405 residence \add ≈to honour me\add*—you've¦197410 shed¦197410 too much¦197409 blood on the ground¦197411 \add ≈in my sight\add*.’
\v 9 \add He told me,\add* ‘Listen, you'll have a¦197416 son¦197416 who'll be¦197417 a¦197421 man¦197421 of¦197421 peace. I'll¦197423 give¦197423 him¦197424 relief from¦197425 all¦197425 his¦197427 enemies¦197427 from¦197428 the surrounding¦197428 regions. That's why he'll¦197420 be¦197431 called¦197432 ‘Shelomoh¦197430’ \add (which sounds like ‘Shalom’—the Hebrew word for peace)\add*, and¦197433 I'll¦197435 give peace¦197433 and¦197434 quietness¦197434 to¦197436 Yisrael¦197438 during¦197439 his¦197439 lifetime¦197439.
\v 10 He'll¦197443 be the one to build¦197443 a¦197444 residence for¦197445 me, and¦197446 he himself will¦197447 become¦197447 my son¦197450, and¦197451 I'll¦197451 \add ≡become¦197447\add* his father¦197454, and¦197455 I'll¦197455 establish¦197455 his¦197457 kingdom's¦197457 \add ≈authority\add* over¦197458 Yisrael¦197460 forever¦197463.’
\p
\v 11 “Now¦197465, my¦197466 son¦197466, may¦197467 Yahweh¦197468 be with¦197469 you¦197469, and¦197470 may you¦197470 be¦197470 successful¦197470 and¦197471 build¦197471 a residence for Yahweh¦197473 your¦197474 god¦197474, just¦197475 as¦197475 he¦197476 said¦197476 you¦197477 would.
\v 12 \add ≈I also ask\add* Yahweh to give you¦197482 insight¦197484 and¦197485 understanding¦197485, and¦197486 give you¦197486 charge¦197486 over¦197487 Yisrael¦197489 so¦197490 that you can keep¦197490 your¦197495 god¦197495 Yahweh's¦197494 regulations.
\v 13 Then¦197497 you'll¦197498 succeed¦197498, if¦197499 you're¦197501 careful¦197501 to follow the¦197505 instructions and¦197506 the¦197508 directions that¦197509 Yahweh¦197511 commanded¦197510 Mosheh¦197514 \add !(Moses¦197514)\add* concerning Yisrael¦197517. Be¦197518 strong¦197518 and¦197519 courageous¦197519. Don't¦197520 be¦197522 afraid¦197522 or discouraged¦197525.\x + \xo 22:13: \xt Josh 1:6-9.\x*
\p
\v 14 Now, see¦197527, \add ?≈despite many battles\add*, I've¦197529 prepared¦197529 the¦197530 following for¦197530 Yahweh's¦197532 residence: three thousand tonnes of gold¦197533 and thirty thousand tonnes of silver¦197538, along with too much bronze¦197542 and¦197543 iron¦197543 to¦197547 weigh¦197545, and¦197549 timber¦197549 and¦197550 \add cut\add* stones¦197550. Plus¦197552 you'll¦197553 be able to¦197552 add¦197553 more.
\v 15 \add ≈You'll¦197555 have plenty of¦197557 skilled¦197565 workers¦197557, including those who work¦197558 with stone¦197561 and¦197562 those who work with wood¦197562\add*.
\v 16 \add ≈Then there's¦197574 so many skilled with gold¦197570 and silver¦197571, and¦197572 bronze¦197572 and¦197573 iron¦197573. So get organised and¦197577 get started\add*, and¦197578 may Yahweh¦197579 be with¦197580 you¦197580.
\p
\v 17 Then¦197582 David¦197583 ordered¦197582 all¦197584 the¦197586 Israeli¦197587 officials¦197586 to¦197588 assist¦197588 his¦197590 son¦197590 Shelomoh¦197589 \add !(Solomon¦197589)\add*, \add saying\add*,
\v 18 “Isn't¦197592 Yahweh¦197593 your¦197594 god¦197594 with¦197595 you¦197595 \add officials\add*, and¦197596 hasn't he¦197596 given¦197596 you¦197597 peace \add ≈on every side\add*? He's¦197601 \add ≈allowed me to take control of this region¦197605, and¦197606 this area has¦197606 been¦197606 subdued¦197606 with the¦197608 help\add* of¦197608 Yahweh¦197609 and¦197610 his¦197611 people¦197611.
\v 19 Now¦197613, \add ≈dedicate your¦197615 minds¦197615 and¦197616 strength to¦197617 requesting¦197617 advice from your god Yahweh¦197618, then¦197620 get organised and¦197621 build¦197621 Yahweh¦197625 God's sanctuary¦197624 so you can bring¦197627 the¦197630 box¦197630 containing Yahweh's¦197633 agreement¦197631 to the¦197636 residence to¦197637 be¦197638 built¦197638 to honour Yahweh's¦197641 name¦197639, and bring God's sacred¦197635 items¦197634\add*.”
\c 23
