\v 4 \add David assigned\add* twenty-four thousand of them to¦197682 supervise the¦197685 work¦197685 at Yahweh's¦197688 residence, six¦197694 thousand¦197691 to be¦197692 officials¦197692 and¦197693 judges¦197693,
\v 5 four¦197697 thousand¦197698 to be¦197699 gatekeepers¦197699, and¦197700 four¦197700 thousand¦197701 to¦197703 praise¦197707 Yahweh¦197703 using the musical instruments¦197704 that¦197705 he'd provided.
\p
\v 6 \add ≈So¦197709\add* David¦197710 divided¦197709 \add @the¦197709 Levites¦197709\add* into divisions¦197711 according to¦197713 \add their ancestry through\add* Levi's¦197714 sons¦197713 Gereshon¦197715, Kohat¦197716, and¦197717 Merari¦197717.
\s1 The Gershonim
\rem /s1 The Gershonites; Gershonites
\p
\v 7 The Gershonim \add included\add* Laedan¦197721 and¦197722 Shimei¦197722.
\v 8 Laedan's¦197726 three¦197731 sons¦197725 were¦197727: Yehiel¦197728 (the oldest), Zetam¦197729, and¦197730 Yoel¦197730 \add !(Joel¦197730)\add*.
\v 9 Shimei's¦197735\f + \fr 23:9 \ft Possibly the wrong name got into the Hebrew here, because it disagrees with v10.\f* three¦197740 sons¦197734 were¦197736: Shelomot, Haziel¦197738, and¦197739 Haran¦197739. (They were¦197742 leaders of¦197744 Laedan's¦197744 clans.)
\v 10 Shimei's¦197748 four¦197757 sons were¦197749: Yahat¦197749, Zina¦197750,\f + \fr 23:10 \ft Some ancient translations have Zizah here, which would seem to fit better with v11.\f* Ye'ush¦197751, and¦197752 Beriah¦197752.
\v 11 (Yahat¦197761 was the¦197762 head¦197762, and¦197763 Zizah¦197763 was second¦197764. Ye'ush¦197765 and¦197766 Beriah¦197766 were¦197771 \add ≈grouped¦197774 together as one¦197775 family¦197772 unit because they¦197769 didn't¦197767 have¦197769 many¦197769 descendants¦197770\add*.)
\s2 The Kohatites
\rem /s1 Kohathites; The Kohathites
\p
\v 12 Kohat's¦197779 four¦197784 sons¦197778 were¦197780: Amram¦197780, Yitshar¦197781, Hevron¦197782, and¦197783 Uziel¦197783.
\v 13 Amram's¦197788 sons¦197787 were¦197789 Aharon¦197789 \add !(Aaron¦197789)\add* and¦197790 Mosheh¦197790 \add !(Moses¦197790)\add*. Aharon¦197792 \add ≈and¦197798 his future male descendants¦197798 were¦197791 permanently appointed\add* to¦197793 consecrate¦197793 the most sacred things, to¦197802 burn incense, to minister¦197805 to Yahweh¦197804, and¦197806 to¦197806 bless¦197806 his¦197807 name¦197807.\x + \xo 23:13: \xt Exo 28:1.\x*
\v 14 Mosheh¦197812 \add was known as\add* \add ≈a man¦197813 who served\add* God, and his¦197815 descendants¦197815 were¦197816 included with the \add other\add* Levites.
\v 15 Mosheh's¦197823 sons¦197822 were¦197824 Gereshom¦197824 and¦197825 Eliezer¦197825.
\v 16 Gereshom's¦197828 eldest \add #son¦197827\add* was¦197829 Shevuel¦197829.
\v 17 Eliezer's only son¦197833 was¦197832 Rehavyah¦197836, but Rehavyah¦197845 \add went on to\add* have many sons.
\p
\v 18 Yitshar's¦197850 eldest \add #son¦197849\add* was¦197851 Shelomot.
\v 19 Hevron's¦197856 sons¦197855 \add ≈from oldest to youngest\add* were¦197857: Yeriyah¦197857, Amaryah¦197859, Yahaziel¦197861, and¦197863 Yekameam¦197863.
\v 20 Uziel's¦197867 sons¦197866 were¦197868 Mikah¦197868 and¦197870 Yishiyah¦197870.
