\p
\v 21 Merari's¦197875 sons were¦197876 Mahli¦197876 and¦197877 Mushi¦197877, \add and\add* Mahli's¦197879 sons were¦197880 Eleazar¦197880 and¦197881 Kish¦197881.
\v 22 Eleazar¦197884 died¦197883 without having any sons, \add so\add* his brother Kish's¦197897 sons married his daughters¦197893 \add (to continue the family name)\add*.
\v 23 Mushi¦197901 had three¦197905 sons¦197900: Mahli¦197902, Eder¦197903, and¦197904 Yerimot¦197904.
\p
\v 24 Those¦197907 were¦197908 Levi's¦197910 descendants¦197908 \add ≈by¦197916 their clans and their appointments, who did the work¦197920 of serving¦197921 in Yahweh's¦197923 residence once they reached twenty¦197925 years¦197926 old\add*,
\v 25 because¦197929 David¦197931 had¦197930 said¦197930, “Yisrael's¦197936 \add !(Israel¦197936)\add* god¦197934 Yahweh¦197933 has¦197932 given¦197932 peace to¦197937 his¦197937 people¦197937, and¦197938 he'll¦197938 \add now\add* live forever¦197942 in¦197939 Yerushalem¦197939 \add !(Jerusalem¦197939)\add*,
\v 26 \add ≈so¦197944\add* the Levites¦197945 won't¦197946 need to¦197948 carry¦197948 the¦197951 \add ≈sacred¦197951 tent¦197951\add* anymore, along with all¦197954 its equipment¦197956.”\x + \xo 23:26: \xt Deu 10:8.\x*
\v 27 \add ≈So one of¦197960 David's¦197961 final¦197962 instructions had been¦197964 to count¦197964 the¦197965 Levite¦197967 men who were twenty¦197969 years¦197970 old and¦197971 over\add*,
\v 28 because¦197973 their¦197974 work was¦197975 to¦197975 \add ≈assist\add* Aharon's¦197978 \add !(Aaron¦197978)\add* descendants¦197977 in their work¦197979 in Yahweh's¦197981 residence.\x + \xo 23:28-32: \xt Num 3:5-9.\x* They \add ≈were in charge\add* of the¦197984 courtyards¦197984 and siderooms, \add ≈in charge of the purification¦197990 ceremonies\add*, and¦197994 did other work¦197994 at God's¦197993 residence.
\v 29 \add ≡They were also in charge of\add* the¦197999 \add sacred\add* bread¦197999, as well as the¦198000 fine¦198001 flour¦198001 for¦198002 the offering¦198002, the¦198003 wafers¦198003 of¦198003 bread without raising agent, the¦198004 baking pans, and \add ≈all¦198007 the measuring¦198009 and¦198010 mixing of ingredients\add*.
\p
\v 30 Every morning and¦198012 every evening¦198019 \add @the Levites\add* stood¦198012 and¦198016 praised¦198016 Yahweh¦198017.
\v 31 They would also¦198021 do that on the rest days, and at the new moon¦198026 celebrations and¦198027 during the other religious festivals¦198027. \add ≈There were regulations¦198029 about how many¦198021 of them¦198030 must always¦198031 be on duty serving\add* Yahweh¦198033.
\v 32 They¦198035 were \add also\add* \add ≈in charge of¦198038\add* the¦198039 sacred tent¦198039 and¦198042 the¦198044 holy¦198044 place¦198044, and¦198045 assisting \add the priests\add* (their¦198048 relatives¦198048, Aharon's¦198047 descendants¦198046) in their service¦198049 at Yahweh's¦198051 residence.
\c 24
