\rem /s1 The Work Assigned to the Priests; Duties of the Priests; Divisions of the Priests; The Divisions of Priests
\s4 Full kingdom
\p
\v 1 Aharon's¦198055 \add !(Aaron¦198055)\add* sons¦198057 were¦198059: Nadav¦198059, Avihu¦198060, Eleazar¦198061, and¦198062 Itamar¦198062,
\v 2 \add ≈but¦198064\add* Nadav¦198065 and¦198066 Avihu¦198066 died¦198064 \add ≈before¦198067 their father¦198068\add* and¦198069 \add ≈without having any children¦198069,\x + \xo 24:2: \xt Lev 10:1-2.\x* so¦198074\add* \add only\add* Eleazar¦198075 and¦198076 Itamar¦198076 became priests¦198074.
\v 3 David¦198079 \add ≈gave Eleazar's¦198084 descendant Tsadok¦198080, and¦198085 Itamar's¦198089 descendant Ahimelek¦198085 two different sets of duties to¦198090 perform\add*.
\v 4 \add ≈There were¦198093 more¦198100 leaders among Eleazar's¦198096 descendants than¦198100 there were among Itamar's¦198103 descendants, so¦198104 they¦198104 appointed sixteen leaders from Eleazar's¦198106 descendants and eight¦198117 from Itamar's¦198114 descendants\add*.
\v 5 They¦198119 divided¦198119 up \add ≈the duties by¦198120 a process of¦198128 choosing randomly, so¦198131 some of the¦198131 leaders¦198131 from¦198133 each of¦198131 the¦198132 two groups served the¦198133 facility and¦198135 others served God directly\add*. DOUBLE-CHECK, along with verse 3 as well.
\v 6 Netanel's¦198143 son Shemayah¦198140 was the Levite scribe¦198144 who recorded¦198139 all this in¦198148 front¦198148 of¦198148 the¦198149 king¦198149 and¦198150 the¦198150 leaders¦198150, Tsadok¦198151 the¦198152 priest¦198152 and¦198153 Evyatar's¦198156 son Ahimelek¦198153, and¦198157 the¦198157 clan leaders of¦198157 the¦198158 priests¦198159 and¦198160 the Levites¦198160. (One¦198164 \add ≈family¦198161\add* from Eleazar's¦198166 group was randomly assigned a duty, and¦198167 then one from Itamar's¦198170 group, and so on.)
\p
\v 7 The¦198175 first¦198175 two \add ≈allocations of duties\add* went¦198173 to¦198176 Yehoyariv¦198176 and then Yedayah¦198177.
\v 8 Next were Harim¦198180 and Se'orim¦198182,
\v 9 Malkiyah¦198185 and Miyamin¦198187,
\v 10 Hakots¦198190 and Aviyah¦198192,
\v 11 Yeshua¦198195 and Shekanyah¦198197,
\v 12 Elyashiv¦198200 and Yakim¦198203,
\v 13 Hupah¦198207 and Yeshev'av,
\v 14 Bilgah¦198214 and Imer¦198217,
\v 15 Hezir¦198221 and Hapitsets¦198224,
\v 16 Petahyah¦198228 and Yehezkel¦198231,
\v 17 Yakin¦198234 and¦198236 Gemul¦198237,
\v 18 Delayah¦198241 and¦198243, lastly, Ma'azyah¦198244.
\p
\v 19 Those¦198249 \add were the priests\add* selected to \add be leaders of the groups\add* that would serve¦198251 in Yahweh's temple¦198253, following the¦198253 instructions¦198261 that Yisrael's¦198264 \add !(Israel¦198264)\add* god¦198263 Yahweh¦198255 had given their¦198256 ancestor¦198259 Aharon¦198258 \add !(Aaron¦198258)\add*.
