\p
\v 1 Then¦198381 David¦198382 and¦198383 the¦198384 army¦198384 chiefs allocated the \add musical\add* service¦198385 to¦198386 the¦198386 sons¦198386 of¦198386 Asaf¦198387, Heyman¦198388, and¦198389 Yedutun¦198389—the ones prophesying¦198390 with¦198393 harps¦198393, with¦198394 lyres¦198394, and¦198395 with¦198395 cymbals¦198395. \add ≈This is¦198396 a list¦198397 of¦198397 the men¦198398 they chose for¦198400 that work¦198400\add*:
\li1
\v 2 From Asaf's¦198403 sons: Zakur¦198404, Yosef¦198405 \add !(Joseph¦198405)\add*, Netanyah¦198406, and¦198407 Asarelah¦198407. They were¦198410 supervised by Asaf¦198413, who¦198414 prophesied¦198414 \add ≈under the king's¦198418 direction\add*.
\li1
