\v 5 They were all¦198461 sons¦198464 of¦198465 King¦198467 David's prophet¦198466 Heyman¦198465, \add ≈who'd been promised¦198468 by¦198468 God that he'd strengthen him\add*, and¦198472 God gave¦198472 \add *him¦198474\add* fourteen sons¦198475 and¦198478 three¦198479 daughters¦198478.
\p
\v 6 All¦198481 of¦198481 those¦198483 served¦198494 as musicians in Yahweh's¦198490 temple under their¦198487 \add #fathers'¦198487\add* supervision—they played cymbals¦198491, harps¦198492, and¦198493 lyres¦198493. \add ≈Their fathers were supervised by\add* the¦198499 king¦198499.
\v 7 There were 288 of¦198506 those men and their¦198506 musical relatives¦198509 who¦198510 played to¦198513 Yahweh¦198513.
\v 8 They¦198521 used \add ≈a process of choosing randomly\add* to determine \add &their\add* \add #duties¦198523\add*, whether young or old, and \add ≈irrespective of¦198524 their musical abilities\add*.
\p
