\v 11 Hilkiyah¦198846, Tevalyah¦198848, and Zekaryah¦198850 \add !(Zechariah¦198850)\add*. (Thirteen sons¦198854 and¦198855 relatives¦198855 in total¦198852.)
\p
\v 12 Those¦198860 men were leaders¦198863 of¦198861 the groups¦198861 of¦198863 men who guarded the temple's gates. They worked in¦198869 Yahweh's¦198870 temple¦198869 like¦198866 their¦198867 relatives¦198867 did.
\v 13 \add ≈They¦198872 used a process of choosing randomly to¦198876 assign each family¦198876 to a particular gate, irrespective of the family reputation\add*.
\v 14 Shelemyah's¦198885 group was allocated to the¦198883 eastern¦198884 gate, and¦198886 his¦198887 son¦198887 Zekaryah¦198886 (a¦198888 wise adviser) was allocated to the northern¦198895 gate.
\v 15 Oved¦198898-Edom's group was allocated to¦198900 the¦198900 southern¦198900 gate, plus¦198901 his¦198901 sons¦198901 \add were to guard\add* the storehouses¦198903.
\v 16 Shupim's¦198905 and¦198906 Hosah's¦198906 groups were allocated the¦198909 western gate¦198909, along¦198914 with the Shaleket¦198910 gate on¦198911 the uphill road¦198911, with \add ≈side-by-side guards\add*.
\v 17 Every day there were six¦198919 Levites¦198918 on duty in the east¦198917, four in the north¦198920, four¦198922 in the south¦198923, and¦198926 two at the storehouses¦198926.
\v 18 There were four¦198932 on the road¦198933 by the western courtyard, and two¦198934 in the courtyard.
\v 19 Those¦198937 were¦198938 the¦198938 groups¦198938 of men who were Korah's and¦198942 Merari's¦198943 descendants who guarded the \add temple\add* gates.
