\v 24 Shuvael, a descendant of¦198986 Mosheh's¦198988 \add !(Moses¦198988)\add* son Gereshom¦198985, was¦198989 \add another\add* leader¦198989 \add ≈in charge of\add* the¦198992 treasuries¦198992,
\v 25 along with his¦198994 relatives¦198994: Eliezer's¦198995 son Rehavyah¦198996, \add @Rehavyah's\add* son Yeshayah¦198998 \add !(Isaiah¦198998)\add*, \add @Yeshayah's\add* son Yoram¦199000 \add !(Joram¦199000)\add*, \add @Yoram's¦199001\add* son¦199001 Zikri¦199002, and¦199004 \add @Zikri's¦199006\add* son¦199006 Shelomot.
\v 26 Shelomot¦199009 and¦199010 his¦199010 relatives¦199010 \add ≈supervised\add* all¦199012 the¦199014 storehouses¦199014 for the¦199015 sacred¦199015 things¦199015 that¦199016 were consecrated¦199017 by King¦199019 David¦199018, the \add ≈clan leaders\add*, and¦199025 the¦199027 army¦199027 division leaders and other commanders¦199026
\v 27 who'd dedicated¦199035 some¦199029 of¦199029 the¦199034 plunder¦199034 \add ≈from their battles¦199031\add* to¦199036 the repair¦199036 of¦199037 Yahweh's¦199038 residence.
\v 28 ⇔Shelomot and his¦199062 relatives¦199062 were also \add ≈in charge of\add* everything that¦199041 the¦199043 prophet¦199043 Shmuel¦199042 \add !(Samuel¦199042)\add*, \add King\add* Sha'ul¦199044 \add !(Saul¦199044)\add* (Kish's¦199047 son), and¦199048 \add David's two army commanders\add* Avner¦199048 (Ner's¦199051 son) and¦199052 Yoav¦199052 \add !(Joab¦199052)\add* (Tseruyah's¦199055 son) had dedicated¦199057 \add to Yahweh\add*.
