\p
\v 1 \add ≈Now\add* David¦199668 called all¦199671 of¦199671 Yisrael's¦199674 \add !(Israel¦199674)\add* leaders to assemble¦199667 in Yerushalem¦199706 \add !(Jerusalem¦199706)\add*: the tribal leaders, the leaders of¦199677 the¦199678 \add various\add* divisions¦199678 that¦199679 served¦199679 the¦199682 king¦199682, the¦199683 commanders¦199683 of¦199683 army units of thousands¦199684 and¦199685 of¦199685 hundreds¦199686, and¦199687 the¦199687 supervisors of¦199687 all¦199688 the¦199690 property¦199690 and¦199692 cattle¦199692 belonging to¦199694 the¦199694 king¦199694 and¦199695 his¦199695 sons¦199695, along with¦199696 the¦199698 top officials¦199698, and¦199699 the¦199699 warriors¦199699, including¦199700 \add ≈their powerful heroes\add*.
\p
\v 2 Then¦199708 King¦199710 David¦199709 stood up¦199708 and¦199714 spoke¦199714, “Listen¦199715 to¦199715 me¦199715, my¦199716 brothers¦199716 and¦199717 my¦199717 people¦199717, I¦199718 wanted in my¦199721 heart¦199721 to¦199722 put up a¦199723 building for¦199725 the¦199725 box¦199725 containing Yahweh's¦199728 agreement¦199726 to rest¦199724 in. It's the¦199729 footstool¦199729 for our¦199731 god's¦199731 feet, and¦199732 I've¦199732 made preparations¦199732 to¦199733 start building¦199733,\x + \xo 28:2-7: \xt 2Sam 7:1-16; 1Ch 17:1-14.\x*
\v 3 but¦199735 God¦199735 told¦199736 me¦199737 that \add %I¦199740\add* wouldn't be the one to build¦199740 a¦199741 house¦199741 to \add ≈honour him\add*, because¦199742 \add %I've¦199742\add* \add ≈been¦199744 involved in a¦199744 lot of¦199744 war¦199745 and¦199747 killings\add*.
\p
\v 4 “Yet Yisrael's god¦199752 Yahweh¦199751 chose¦199750 me¦199754 from¦199755 all¦199755 of¦199756 my¦199758 father's¦199758 \add ≈family\add* to¦199759 be¦199759 king¦199760 over¦199761 Yisrael¦199763 forever¦199764, because¦199765 he¦199767 chose¦199767 a leader¦199768 from \add the tribe of\add* Yehudah¦199770 \add !(Judah¦199770)\add*, my¦199772 father's¦199772 tribe, and¦199773 among¦199773 my¦199774 father's¦199774 sons¦199773, he¦199776 was pleased¦199776 to¦199777 make¦199777 me¦199777 king¦199777 over¦199778 all¦199780 of¦199780 Yisrael¦199782.
\v 5 Then¦199784 out of the many¦199788 sons¦199789 that \add *he's\add* given¦199790 me¦199791, he¦199793 chose¦199793 my¦199795 son¦199795 Shelomoh¦199794 \add !(Solomon¦199794)\add* to¦199796 \add ≈be the next king to rule his kingdom¦199800 of¦199800\add* Yisrael¦199804.
\p
\v 6 “Then¦199806 he¦199806 told¦199806 me¦199807, ‘Your son Shelomoh¦199808 is the one who'll build¦199812 my¦199813 temple¦199813 and¦199814 the courtyards¦199814 \add around it\add*, because¦199815 I've¦199817 chosen¦199817 him¦199818 to be like my son¦199820, and¦199821 I'll¦199822 be like a¦199825 father¦199825 to him.
\v 7 I'll¦199827 establish¦199827 his¦199830 kingdom¦199830 forever¦199833, if¦199834 he's¦199836 diligent at following my¦199838 instructions¦199838 and¦199839 \add obeying\add* my¦199839 judgements¦199839, like¦199840 he is at present.’
\p
\v 8 “\add ≈So¦199843\add* now¦199843, in \add ≈front\add* of¦199844 all¦199845 of¦199845 Yisrael¦199847, Yahweh's¦199850 assembly¦199848, and¦199851 in¦199851 the¦199851 hearing of¦199851 our¦199852 god¦199852, \add I challenge you all to discover and obey\add* all¦199855 of¦199855 your god Yahweh's¦199858 commands¦199857, so¦199860 that¦199860 you'll¦199861 all possess¦199861 the¦199865 good¦199865 land¦199864, and¦199866 you'll¦199866 leave your¦199867 sons after¦199868 you¦199868 to \add ≈inherit\add* it forever¦199871.
\p
\v 9 “And¦199874 you¦199874, Shelomoh¦199875 my¦199877 son¦199877, \add ≈follow\add* your¦199882 father's¦199882 god¦199881 and¦199883 serve¦199883 him¦199883 with¦199884 a¦199884 whole heart¦199884 and¦199886 with¦199886 a¦199886 willing¦199887 life, because¦199888 Yahweh¦199893 \add ≈looks into\add* all¦199889 hearts¦199891, and¦199894 understands¦199898 all¦199894 \add ≈your motives\add*. If¦199899 you¦199901 look¦199901 for him¦199901, he'll¦199902 \add make sure\add* you¦199903 find¦199902 him, but¦199904 if¦199904 you¦199906 abandon¦199906 him¦199906, he'll¦199907 reject¦199907 you¦199907 forever¦199908.
\v 10 You can now¦199912 see¦199910 that you need to be¦199922 strong¦199922 and get busy, because¦199913 Yahweh¦199915 has¦199916 chosen¦199916 you¦199917 to¦199918 erect a building¦199918 to be \add &his¦199920\add* sanctuary¦199921.”
\p
\v 11 Then¦199926 David¦199927 gave¦199926 the plans for \add the temple\add* to¦199928 his¦199929 son¦199929 Shelomoh¦199928, \add ≡including plans\add* for its porch¦199933, its houses¦199936, its¦199936 treasuries¦199937, its¦199938 upper¦199938 rooms¦199938 and¦199939 its¦199939 inner¦199940 rooms, and¦199941 the¦199941 \add ≈room to contain the¦199942 sacred box\add*.
\v 12 \add He also handed over\add* the¦199944 plans he envisioned for¦199950 the¦199950 temple courtyards¦199950, all¦199954 the¦199956 surrounding¦199957 apartments, all¦199957 the¦199958 treasuries¦199958, and¦199961 all the¦199961 storerooms¦199961 for sacred¦199962 things¦199962.
\v 13 \add He included instructions\add* for¦199964 the¦199964 divisions¦199964 of¦199964 the¦199965 priests¦199965 and¦199966 Levites¦199966, for¦199967 all¦199967 the¦199969 \add ≈services¦199970 required to operate the¦199971 temple¦199971, and¦199974 for¦199974 all¦199974 the¦199976 equipment and utensils needed for all that\add*.
\v 14 \add David had determined\add* the weight¦199983 of¦199984 gold¦199984 and¦199989 silver¦199992 that would be needed to¦199990 make all¦199990 the¦199991 necessary items¦199991 that would be used in the¦199992 regular \add temple\add* functions,
