\p
\v 1 Then¦200138 King¦200140 David¦200139 told¦200138 the¦200140 entire¦200141 assembly¦200143, “My¦200145 son¦200145 Shelomoh¦200144 \add !(Solomon¦200144)\add* \add ≈has¦200147 been chosen¦200147 by God¦200150 himself\add*. He's young¦200151 and¦200152 tender,\x + \xo 29:1-2: \xt 1Ch 22:5.\x* and¦200153 \add ≈it's a huge¦200154 job\add*, because¦200155 the¦200158 temple¦200158 isn't¦200156 being built for¦200159 people¦200157, but for¦200160 Yahweh¦200160 God¦200161.
\v 2 \add ≈I've¦200166 used all my resources to provide a plentiful supply of materials\add* for my¦200169 god's¦200169 residence: the¦200170 gold¦200170 for¦200172 the gold¦200172 things, and¦200173 the¦200173 silver¦200173 for¦200174 the silver¦200174 things, the¦200175 bronze¦200175 for¦200176 the bronze¦200176 things, the¦200177 iron¦200177 for¦200178 the iron¦200178 things, the¦200179 wood¦200179 for¦200180 the wooden¦200180 parts, onyx¦200183 stones¦200185 for inlays, antimony¦200187 stones and¦200188 colourful¦200188 things, and¦200189 all¦200189 the rare stones¦200190, and¦200192 alabaster¦200194 stones.
\v 3 What's more, because¦200198 I'm¦200198 excited to have my¦200200 god's¦200200 residence \add built\add*, I've donated my¦200200 own personal gold¦200205 and¦200206 silver¦200206 on top of everything else that¦200214 I've¦200214 prepared¦200214 for¦200215 the \add ≈sacred¦200216\add* temple:
