\p
\v 6 Then¦200250 the¦200251 family leaders¦200251 and¦200253 the¦200253 leaders¦200253 of¦200253 the¦200255 \add ≈tribes¦200255\add*, and¦200257 the¦200257 \add ≈various levels of military\add* commanders¦200257, and the¦200262 king's¦200262 \add ≈construction overseers\add*, \add all\add* \add ≈contributed¦200250\add* willingly.
\v 7 They¦200264 donated \add a total of\add* 170 tonnes of¦200265 gold and 100kg of gold¦200269 coins, 350 tonnes of¦200271 silver¦200276, 600 tonnes of¦200278 bronze¦200280, and¦200282 3,400 tonnes of¦200282 iron¦200285 for the \add ≈temple¦200266\add* construction,
\v 8 plus¦200291 anyone¦200291 who¦200291 had precious stones¦200293 donated them¦200294 to¦200295 the¦200295 treasury¦200295 for the¦200296 \add ≈temple¦200296\add*. Yehiel¦200302 (a Gershoni) \add ≈was in charge of those\add*.
\v 9 The¦200306 people¦200306 were \add ≈excited\add*, because they'd \add all\add* given willingly to¦200314 Yahweh¦200314, and¦200315 King¦200317 David¦200316 was also¦200315 very pleased.
